  <div class="prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-brand-dark/80 /80 space-y-6">
    <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> October 2026</p>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Welcome to Our Table: Our Privacy Philosophy</h2>
      <p>Let's be incredibly honest for a moment. Nobody actually enjoys reading privacy policies. Usually, they are massive walls of impenetrable legal jargon designed to protect the company, rather than the person reading them. But we want to do things differently here at Calorie Calculator Free.</p>
      <p>Welcome to our site. Your privacy is not just an afterthought or a legal box we are forced to check—it is the foundational pillar of how we build and maintain our software. We intimately understand that physical metrics, such as your current weight, your height, your age, your gender, and your deeply personal health goals, are incredibly sensitive information. This is your body we are talking about. In an era where data brokering has become a multi-billion dollar industry and unauthorized data sharing is far too common, we have chosen to take a fundamentally different path.</p>
      <p>Our philosophy is simple: Your health data belongs to you. Not to us, not to advertisers, and certainly not to obscure third-party data brokers. This Privacy Policy outlines exactly what information we interact with, how we use it, and, most importantly, what we actively refuse to collect when you use our tools at caloriecalculatorfree.com. By choosing to use our website, you are agreeing to the terms outlined below, but more importantly, you are entering into a relationship of trust with us. We do not take that trust lightly.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. The Data We Do NOT Collect (Our Client-Side Promise)</h2>
      <p>If you have used other health and fitness applications in the past, you are probably used to the standard drill: create an account, verify your email, log in, and upload all your personal body metrics to a remote database in the cloud. We completely reject that model.</p>
      <p>Instead, we employ a strict"Client-Side First" architecture for every single calculator and tool on our platform. But what does that actually mean for you?</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No Server Transmission:</strong> When you input your age, biological sex, height, and weight into our <a href="/">Calorie Calculator</a>, <a href="/tdee-calculator/">TDEE Calculator</a>, or any other tool on this site, that data is processed entirely within your own web browser. It happens right there on your phone or your computer. The math is done locally.</li>
        <li><strong>No Health Data Storage:</strong> Because all the calculations happen directly on your device, we do not transmit your physiological data across the internet to our servers. We do not have a database filled with our users' weights or calorie goals. In fact, we literally cannot see what you type into the calculator fields. It is a mathematical impossibility for us to access your entries.</li>
        <li><strong>No Account Required:</strong> We don't want your email address. You do not need to create an account, provide a username, or log in to use our core services. The tools are here for you to use freely and anonymously.</li>
      </ul>
      
      <h3>Let's Talk About"Local Storage" (Like Friends)</h3>
      <p>You might notice that we offer a feature allowing you to save your results so that you don't have to re-enter your information every time you visit the site. You might be wondering,"Wait, if you don't save my data on your servers, how does the site remember me?"</p>
      <p>The answer is a web technology called <strong>Local Storage</strong>. Think of Local Storage like a sticky note that you leave on your own refrigerator in your own kitchen. When you hit"Save," our website writes that sticky note and sticks it inside your web browser (like Chrome, Safari, or Edge). We don't get a copy of the sticky note. We don't even know the sticky note exists.</p>
      <p>When you return to the site tomorrow, your browser looks at its own sticky note and fills in the blanks for you. It all stays securely on your physical device. If you ever want to throw that sticky note away, all you have to do is clear your browser's cache or history, and poof—it’s gone forever. You are in complete control.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. The Information We DO Collect (Analytics & Keep-the-Lights-On Data)</h2>
      <p>Okay, we’ve covered what we don't collect. Now, let’s be fully transparent about what we <em>do</em> collect. While your personal health metrics are completely off-limits to us, we do collect standard, non-personally identifiable log data. This is how almost all modern websites operate, and it is necessary to ensure our servers don't crash, our pages load instantly, and we know if people are actually finding our tools useful.</p>
      <p>This standard web traffic data is critical for defending our infrastructure against cyber attacks (like DDoS attacks) and for general site maintenance. This diagnostic and analytical data may include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your IP address (which is anonymized and truncated wherever required by regional laws, so it cannot pinpoint your exact home address).</li>
        <li>Your browser type (e.g., Firefox, Chrome), your operating system (e.g., iOS, Windows), and whether you are browsing on a mobile phone or a desktop computer.</li>
        <li>The specific pages you visit on our domain (for instance, we might see that 5,000 people visited the <a href="/protein-calculator/">Protein Calculator</a> today, and 2,000 visited our <a href="/guides/">Guides section</a>).</li>
        <li>The time and date of your visit, the duration of your stay on those pages, and the referring website that brought you to us (like a Google search or a link from a fitness blog).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To make sense of all this raw traffic data, we utilize industry-standard third-party analytics services, such as Google Analytics and Cloudflare Web Analytics. These tools aggregate the data. We look at the big picture—trends and patterns—not individual users. This helps us vastly improve your user experience. If we see that everyone is struggling to read a certain article, we know we need to rewrite it. If we see the TDEE calculator is getting massive traffic, we know we should dedicate more engineering time to making it even better.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. When You Reach Out to Us: Contact Forms and Emails</h2>
      <p>The only time we ever interact with your personal, identifiable information is when you voluntarily hand it to us. If you encounter a bug, have a suggestion, or just want to say hello, you might choose to contact us via the secure form on our <a href="/contact/">Contact Page</a> or by emailing our support team directly.</p>
      <p>When you do this, you will be providing us with your email address, your name (or whatever nickname you choose to use), and the contents of your message. We want to be crystal clear: we use this information <strong>solely</strong> to respond to your inquiry, troubleshoot your specific technical issue, or gratefully receive your feedback.</p>
      <p>We use a trusted service called Formspree to securely route these contact form submissions directly into our private inbox. We are not in the business of spamming. We will never sell your email address to marketing agencies, data brokers, or third parties. We will not sneakily subscribe you to any promotional newsletters without your explicit, double-opt-in consent. Once we have resolved your support ticket or answered your question, that email thread is securely archived for our records and left alone.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. The Reality of Cookies and Web Beacons</h2>
      <p>Ah, cookies. Not the delicious chocolate chip kind that you might be tracking in our calorie calculator, but the digital kind. We use"cookies"—which are tiny text files placed on your device's hard drive—to collect baseline information, maintain your site preferences (like remembering if you prefer Dark Mode over Light Mode), and generally keep the site running smoothly.</p>
      <p>You have the absolute right to instruct your web browser to refuse all cookies or to indicate when a cookie is being sent. However, please be aware that if you do not accept functional cookies, some minor convenience features of our site might not work as intended. Your theme preference might frustratingly reset to the default every time you reload the page, for instance.</p>
      
      <h3>The Trade-off: Third-Party Ad Networks</h3>
      <p>We believe deeply that health and fitness tools should be accessible to everyone, regardless of their financial situation. To keep this site 100% free and pay for our server costs, domain registration, and development time, we rely on advertising revenue.</p>
      <p>Consequently, third-party vendors, most notably Google, use advertising cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to our website or to other websites across the internet. Google's use of these advertising cookies enables it and its vast network of partners to serve ads that they think are relevant to you based on your browsing history.</p>
      <p>If you find personalized ads creepy or intrusive, you are not alone, and you have power over them. You can easily opt out of personalized advertising by visiting the <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a> page. Alternatively, you can use browser extensions or ad blockers, and while it impacts our revenue, we completely understand and respect your right to use them.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Respecting Your Global Privacy Rights (GDPR, CCPA, and Beyond)</h2>
      <p>We don't care if you live in California, Berlin, Tokyo, or a small town in the Midwest—we respect international privacy frameworks and believe everyone deserves the same high standard of data protection. If you are a resident of the European Economic Area (EEA) under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), a resident of California under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA), or reside in a jurisdiction with similarly robust privacy laws, you are guaranteed specific data protection rights.</p>
      <p>Now, because we fundamentally <strong>do not store personal health data or user accounts</strong>, the actual scope of personal data we hold about anyone is incredibly tiny. However, regarding any data we might incidentally hold (such as an email you sent to our support desk last month), you maintain the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The Right to Access:</strong> You can request a copy of any personal data we may hold about you.</li>
        <li><strong>The Right to Rectification:</strong> You can demand that we correct any inaccurate data we might have.</li>
        <li><strong>The Right to Erasure (The Right to be Forgotten):</strong> You can request that we permanently delete your personal communications with us from our archives.</li>
        <li><strong>The Right to Opt-Out:</strong> You can opt-out of the sale of your personal information. (Note: This is an easy one for us to honor, because we categorically do not and will never sell personal data to anyone, period).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you wish to exercise any of these fundamental rights, please reach out via our Contact Page. We aren't a faceless corporation that will ignore you; we will respond to your request promptly, and certainly within the legally mandated timeframe (which is typically 30 days).</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. Protecting Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>Our tools are designed for adults. Calorie Calculator Free is not intended for, nor is it directed at, children under the age of 13 (or under the age of 16 in some European jurisdictions). Furthermore, from a purely scientific standpoint, nutritional calculations, metabolic rates, and calorie needs for growing adolescents are vastly different than those for adults. Children should not be restricting calories without direct pediatric supervision and guidance from a registered dietitian.</p>
      <p>We do not knowingly collect, solicit, or maintain personally identifiable information from anyone under the age of 13. If you are a parent or guardian and you become aware that your child has provided us with personal data (for example, by reaching out via an email inquiry), please contact us immediately. We will take swift and necessary actions to locate and eradicate that information from our systems.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8. Stepping Outside: Links to Other Sites</h2>
      <p>Throughout our guides, articles, and calculators, you will find links to external, third-party websites. We link to these sites—such as the National Institutes of Health (NIH), the Mayo Clinic, PubMed, or the World Health Organization (WHO)—to provide authoritative educational citations, further reading, and scientific backing for our claims.</p>
      <p>However, once you click a link and leave Calorie Calculator Free, our privacy policy no longer applies. We have absolutely no control over, and assume zero responsibility for, the content, privacy policies, trackers, or practices of any third-party sites or services. We strongly advise you to put on your critical thinking hat and read the privacy policy of every site you visit.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>9. Policy Updates and Changes</h2>
      <p>The internet moves fast, laws change, and sometimes we add new features to the site. As a result, we may need to update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in legal requirements, upgrades to our technical infrastructure, or shifts in our business practices.</p>
      <p>When we make significant changes, we won't hide them. We will notify you by posting the newly revised Privacy Policy directly on this page and updating the"Effective Date" prominently at the very top of the document.</p>
      <p>We encourage you to review this Privacy Policy periodically for any changes. Any modifications to this policy become effective the moment they are posted on this page.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>10. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) About Your Privacy</h2>
      <p>We know that privacy policies can be overwhelming. To make things as clear as possible, we’ve compiled a list of the most common questions our users ask regarding their data, security, and anonymity.</p>
      
      <div class="space-y-4 mt-6">
        <details class="bg-canvas-soft p-4 rounded-lg cursor-pointer">
          <summary class="font-bold text-lg">Can you see how much I weigh?</summary>
          <p class="mt-2">Absolutely not. We do not have access to your weight, height, age, or gender. When you type those numbers into the calculator, the mathematical formula runs exclusively inside your own web browser. The data never travels across the internet to our servers. Your physical metrics are completely invisible to us.</p>
        </details>
        
        <details class="bg-canvas-soft p-4 rounded-lg cursor-pointer">
          <summary class="font-bold text-lg">If I use the"Save Results" feature, where does my data go?</summary>
          <p class="mt-2">It goes nowhere! It stays exactly where it is: on your device. We use a technology called Local Storage, which acts like a tiny, private filing cabinet inside your specific web browser (like Safari or Chrome). We do not have the keys to that filing cabinet. You can empty it anytime by clearing your browser's history and cache.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-canvas-soft p-4 rounded-lg cursor-pointer">
          <summary class="font-bold text-lg">Do you sell my data to health insurance companies or data brokers?</summary>
          <p class="mt-2">Never. We cannot sell what we do not possess. Because we do not collect your personal health metrics, we have nothing to sell to insurance companies, pharmaceutical brands, or data brokers. Our business model relies on standard display advertising, not on exploiting your personal information.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-canvas-soft p-4 rounded-lg cursor-pointer">
          <summary class="font-bold text-lg">Why do I see ads for things I was just searching for?</summary>
          <p class="mt-2">Our site uses third-party advertising networks (primarily Google Ads) to keep our tools free. These networks use their own cookies to display ads that they determine are relevant to your interests, based on your browsing history across the broader internet. We do not provide these ad networks with your calculator inputs. You can opt out of personalized ads directly through Google's Ad Settings.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-canvas-soft p-4 rounded-lg cursor-pointer">
          <summary class="font-bold text-lg">Do I need to accept cookies to use the calculator?</summary>
          <p class="mt-2">No, you do not. The core functionality of the calculators will work perfectly fine even if you block all cookies. However, some minor convenience features—such as remembering your preference for Dark Mode or saving your calculator inputs for your next visit—rely on cookies or Local Storage and will not function if they are blocked.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-canvas-soft p-4 rounded-lg cursor-pointer">
          <summary class="font-bold text-lg">How can I contact you about a privacy concern?</summary>
          <p class="mt-2">We welcome all questions and concerns regarding your privacy. You can reach out to our team at any time by visiting our <a href="/contact/">Contact Page</a>. We review every message personally and strive to respond to all legitimate privacy inquiries as swiftly as possible.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="italic mt-8 text-sm opacity-80">At the end of the day, we are just a team of health enthusiasts and developers who want to provide helpful, free tools without compromising your right to digital privacy. Thank you for trusting us with your time and for using Calorie Calculator Free.</p>
  </div>
